            "title": "Alibaba's cloud business launches second data centre in Dubai",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "DUBAI (Reuters) -Chinese e-commerce giant Alibaba's cloud business unit has launched its second data centre in Dubai, it said on Tuesday, nine years after its first, as it expands its global cloud computing services to meet growing demand.  Alibaba Cloud, the digital technology and artificial intelligence division, said in a statement the launch was part of the technology major's pledge to invest 380 billion yuan ($53 billion) over three years.  \"The Middle East's advantageous position in fast-tracking AI adoption and its collaborative ecosystem are crucial enablers for private and public sector companies to thrive,\" said Eric Wan, vice president of Alibaba Cloud International and regional general manager at Alibaba Cloud Intelligence.",
